# Community Publication Custom Pages

## Context

Proposal, showcase, and event bodies currently store a page-section JSON array in
`community_publications.body`, but they are not real custom pages. Authors cannot
open the regular custom-page route, use the natural page builder after creation,
or manage the page through the standard ownership UI. Detail routes also constrain
the document to the comfortable submodule measure.

## Goal

- Create one owned custom page transactionally for every community publication.
- Create one author-owned forum thread in the same transaction and retain it as
  the publication's required, unique discussion reference.
- Make that page's `pages.content` document the only authored body authority.
- Render the linked document at the full community module width while retaining
  proposal/showcase/event workflow, media, schedule, and attendance UI around it.
- Give authorized users direct View page and Manage page paths using the existing
  `/page/:slug` builder and `/form/page/:slug/manage` routes.
- Give every visible publication a View discussion path and give the thread owner
  or a forum editor the existing `/edit-thread/:threadId` path.
- Preserve visibility, lifecycle, migration parity, and existing publication data.
- Match GWP's owner-or-granular-permission control model for publication edit,
  delete, workflow moderation, participation, and linked-page management.
- Keep comfortable submodule forms centered within the shared shell on every
  viewport without route-specific alignment overrides.

## Non-Goals

- Replacing community detail routes with redirects.
- Copying workflow records into page content.
- Building a second page editor or ownership system.

## Steps

1. Add a forward migration and fresh-schema parity for the publication-to-page
   relationship, including deterministic backfill of existing bodies and owners.
2. Create publication and custom-page rows atomically; project the linked page
   identity/content through visibility-aware community reads.
3. Render the linked document full-width inside community detail and expose the
   canonical view/manage actions only where appropriate.
4. Add backend/frontend regression coverage and reconcile durable specs.
5. Add service-owned edit/delete capability projection, granular manage-others
   permissions, authenticated controls, and centered comfortable-shell geometry.
6. Reconcile community typography and compact actions with forum/page surfaces;
   bind workflow voting, moderation, and attendance to the shared interactive
   section renderer while retaining community tables as the sole domain state.
7. Replace optional external discussion references with transactionally created,
   author-owned threads; backfill safe existing ownership, couple lifecycle, and
   expose canonical view/edit-thread actions.

## Verification

- Backend community and page tests, then `JWT_SECRET=test-secret go test ./...`.
- Frontend focused community tests, full tests, lint, TypeScript, and build.
- Migration ordering/parity, todo pairing, spec references, and `git diff --check`.

